WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.700
Secure logging in C# and ASP.NET Core is a repeatable workflow.

2
00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:08.440
Start by deciding which events matter.

3
00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:25.340
Authentication, authorization, administrative actions, sensitive data access, configuration changes, lifecycle events, dependency failures, and important business outcomes should be considered deliberately rather than added as scattered debug text.

4
00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:30.020
Use structured, consistent, correlation-friendly logging.

5
00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:42.120
Stable event names, message templates, categories, scopes, and safe identifiers such as ExampleRequestId and ExampleCorrelationId make logs easier to query and safer to use.

6
00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:50.140
Consistency across middleware, controllers, services, background jobs, and outbound clients helps investigations.

7
00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:53.460
Keep secrets and sensitive data out of logs.

8
00:00:53.560 --> 00:01:06.440
Do not log passwords, tokens, cookies, keys, connection strings, full request bodies, sensitive headers, uploaded file contents, or raw private records.

9
00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:14.940
Use redaction, minimization, placeholders, and stable identifiers before data reaches broad storage or export paths.

10
00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:17.300
Protect logs after creation.

11
00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:28.840
Apply access control, retention, transport protection, storage review, export controls, dashboard permissions, and integrity expectations according to log purpose.

12
00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:35.820
Audit logs and incident-response logs may require stronger handling than short-lived diagnostics.

13
00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:40.420
Finally, turn logs into monitored signals and improve through review.

14
00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:49.720
Tune alerts, write runbooks, protect evidence, learn from incidents, and update logging conventions as the application changes.

15
00:01:49.820 --> 00:01:54.460
Good logging helps teams operate with clarity without creating unnecessary exposure.
